WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.360
A private security operations dashboard should support decisions, not merely display data.

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:09.080
Start with the questions authorized users must answer and the actions they need to take.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.430
Then select views, measures,

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:14.705
and workflows that make significant events and monitoring failures easy to recognize.

00:00:14.705 --> 00:00:18.700
Combine useful inputs such as CCTV events, local vision alerts, endpoints,

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:24.160
network activity, authentication, vulnerabilities, assets, sensors, and incident notes.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.738
Normalize shared fields while preserving original evidence and source context.

00:00:27.738 --> 00:00:30.473
Distinguish a quiet environment from a broken collection path.

00:00:30.473 --> 00:00:34.960
Effective triage considers impact, confidence, evidence, asset importance, and urgency.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.600
Group related activity, document human decisions,

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.685
and feed false-positive outcomes back into careful tuning.

00:00:40.685 --> 00:00:44.230
Do not let uncertain automation make high-impact judgments about people.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:47.090
Privacy, role-based access, data minimization, retention,

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:49.525
and audit logging belong in the design.

00:00:49.525 --> 00:00:52.940
Reliability requires health monitoring, capacity management, tested backups,

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.985
fallback procedures, and controlled updates.

00:00:54.985 --> 00:00:59.350
The dashboard itself needs authentication, patching, segmentation, protected secrets,

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:00.800
and secure remote access.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:04.400
The end state is practical situational awareness under accountable human control.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:08.660
A well-designed private dashboard helps people review evidence and respond responsibly

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.135
while preserving resilience,

00:01:10.135 --> 00:01:11.570
limiting unnecessary collection,

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:14.510
and protecting the sensitive information entrusted to the system.
